<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russo-Circassian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1763">1763</a>–<a href="/years/1864">1864</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russo-Circassian War was the long struggle of the Circassian peoples of the north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> against Russian conquest, usually dated from 1763 to 1864. Russian forts, raids and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockades</a> wore down the Circassian principalities and tribes. The war ended in 1864 with the expulsion of most <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Circassians</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, in which hundreds of thousands died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russo-circassian-war.jpg" alt="Russo-Circassian War" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heinrich Ambros Eckert · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heinrich_Ambrose_Eckert_-_Battle_between_Cossacks_and_Circassians_(1838).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
